[Better Approach - 2] Using Bottom-Up DP (Tabulation) - O(n x W) Time and O(n x W) SpaceIn the recursive solution, two parameters change: the number of items and the knapsack capacity. These parameters range from 0 to n and 0 to W, respectively. Therefore, we create a 2D array dp[][] of size (n+1) × (W+1), where dp[i][j] stores the maximum value that can be obtained using the first i items with a knapsack capacity of j. The table is first initialized for the base cases when i = 0 or j = 0. After that, the remaining entries are filled using the recursive formula.For each item i and knapsack capacity j, we decide whether to pick the item or not. If we don't pick the item: dp[i][j] remains same as the previous item, that is dp[i - 1][j]. If we pick the item: dp[i][j] is updated to val[i] + dp[i - 1][j - wt[i]].
